{
  "id": 505305673,
  "iid": 25730,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "DVB-S2-BB: Fix CNI field encoding in Mode Adaptation Header",
  "description": "**Summary**\n\nThe CNI (Carrier to Noise plus Interference) field in the DVB-S2 Mode Adaptation Header is decoded in `epan/dissectors/packet-dvb-s2-bb.c` using a `value_string` table (`modeadapt_esno`) whose values were derived from the SatLabs document rather than from the normative ETSI standard. Its encoding does not match ETSI EN 302 307-1, which is already listed as this dissector's normative reference.\n\n**Bug: CNI value mapping does not match ETSI EN 302 307-1**\n\nIn `epan/dissectors/packet-dvb-s2-bb.c`:\n\n`static const value_string modeadapt_esno[] = {\n    {  0, \"modem unlocked, SNR not available\"},\n    {  1, \"-1.000\"},\n    {  2, \"-0.875\"},\n    ...\n    {  9, \"0.000\"},\n    ...\n    {255, \">30.750\"},\n    {  0, NULL}\n};`\n\n**Fix**\n\n`static const value_string modeadapt_esno[] = {\n    {  0, \"-2.0\"},\n    {  1, \"-1.9\"},\n    {  2, \"-1.8\"},\n    ...\n    { 20, \"0.0\"},\n    ...\n    {255, \">23.5\"},\n    {  0, NULL}\n};`\n\nETSI EN 302 307-1 specifies:\n\n> CNI format shall be:\n> CNI = 20 + 10 {10 Log_10[C / (N + I)]} (positive integer, 8 bits, in the range 0 to 255).\n> In fact for DVB-S2 10 Log_10[C / (N + I)] may be in the range -2 dB to +23,5 dB.\n\n\n**Standard reference**\n\nETSI EN 302 307-1 - Digital Video Broadcasting (DVB); Second generation framing structure, channel coding and modulation systems for Broadcasting, Interactive Services, News Gathering and other broadband satellite applications (DVB-S2) - Annex D.5 Signalling of reception quality via return channel (Normative for ACM).\n\n**Impact**\n\n* CNI values are now decoded per the normative ETSI EN 302 307-1 formula instead of the SatLabs reference.\n* Removed the stale comment pointing to the SatLabs PDF link.\n\nFixes: #21385",
  "state": "merged",
